{"id":"7328203796df129b","group":"68","path":"68/68-thm-analytical-level-inclusion.md","title":"Inclusions Between Analytical Levels","display":"thm-analytical-level-inclusion — Inclusions Between Analytical Levels","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-thm-analytical-level-inclusion","aliases":["68-thm-analytical-level-inclusion"],"display":"thm-analytical-level-inclusion — Inclusions Between Analytical Levels","depends_on":["[[68-df-analytical-hierarchy]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"19.2 p.73 / PDF 82","verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source-argument-and-level-zero-extension-reviewed"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-thm-analytical-level-inclusion"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-thm-analytical-level-inclusion</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-analytical-level-inclusion — Inclusions Between Analytical Levels"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4eb7f663287e8b98\" href=\"?note=4eb7f663287e8b98\" title=\"68-df-analytical-hierarchy\">68-df-analytical-hierarchy</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"19.2 p.73 / PDF 82"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-argument-and-level-zero-extension-reviewed"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m,k,n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(m,k,n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>；各元数的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Delta_n^{1,(m,k)}\">\\(\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Delta_n^{1,(m,k)}\\)</span> 及第零层算术辅助约定见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4eb7f663287e8b98\" href=\"?note=4eb7f663287e8b98\" title=\"68-df-analytical-hierarchy\">68-df-analytical-hierarchy</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)}\\cup\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)}\\subseteq\\Delta_{n+1}^{1,(m,k)}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)}\\cup\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)}\\subseteq\\Delta_{n+1}^{1,(m,k)}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书19.2陈述正层级包含；本处也包括第零层辅助约定。把哑实量词加在前缀前后给相邻层两个方向的包含，同类相邻实量词用一个实数编码合并。第零层算术关系添加一个不出现的实存在或实全称量词即进入两种第一层。已核对PDF82原页陈述及证明路线；没有断言相邻层相等。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-analytical-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"4eb7f663287e8b98","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-analytical-hierarchy]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-analytical-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"4eb7f663287e8b98","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$m,k,n\\in\\mathbb N$；各元数的 $\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Delta_n^{1,(m,k)}$ 及第零层算术辅助约定见 [[68-df-analytical-hierarchy]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"m,k,n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)},\\Delta_n^{1,(m,k)}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma_n^{1,(m,k)}\\cup\\Pi_n^{1,(m,k)}\\subseteq\\Delta_{n+1}^{1,(m,k)}.","display":true}],"bytes":1252,"backlinks":[{"id":"038e64585683402b","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"be41c4d7dd143cb1","anchor":"ref-109","locations":["正文"],"